# Named after the Dockerfile and co-located with it, not at the context
# root -- BuildKit looks for <dockerfile-name>.dockerignore next to the
# Dockerfile itself, in addition to a plain .dockerignore at the context
# root, so this still applies even though the build context is the repo
# root (see docker-compose.yml's `context: ..`). The image only needs
# Setup-Packages/requirements-docker.txt and GitStone-Packages/gitstone.py,
# so everything else below is excluded. Note GitStone-Packages/ itself is
# NOT excluded wholesale: gitstone.py and gitstone_webui/ are siblings in
# there now, and only the latter (the web UI, not needed by this image) is
# excluded -- verified that excluding a subdirectory doesn't drop its
# sibling file.
.git/
.github/
Docker-Packages/
GitStone-Packages/gitstone_webui/
tests/
*.md
LICENSE
pyproject.toml
setup.cfg
Setup-Packages/requirements-local.txt

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
build/
dist/
